# Copy to mobile/.env (gitignored) and fill in. Names only — no values here.
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* at BUILD time, so both of these are baked into the
# binary: they are public by construction, and the Maps key is protected by its
# restrictions in Google Cloud rather than by secrecy. Anything that must stay
# secret does not belong in this file or in this app.

# Google Maps / Places, read by app.config.js (android.config.googleMaps and
# extra.googleMapsApiKey) and used by LocationPicker's autocomplete + details
# calls. The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix is load-bearing: without it app.config.js reads
# undefined, extra.googleMapsApiKey becomes an empty string, and every Places
# request comes back REQUEST_DENIED (TODO-24 — this template named the variable
# without the prefix, so filling it in produced a build with no key at all).
# Restrict the key to the package name com.damiprod.ecotrack plus the release
# signing SHA-1 before using it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE

# Which backend the build talks to, read by constants/ApiConfig.ts. Unset, it
# falls back to the old hardcoded http://146.190.224.202:8080/api — a droplet
# that no longer answers — so a new build should always set this to the HTTPS
# domain. Kept as a fallback only because installed builds depend on it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://your-domain.example/api
